>
> Yes, but this only works while it's wielded, and because it's an
> artifact this eats your main weapon slot.  Wizards automatically have
> three MR items and only one of those needs to be wielded and their quest
> artifact doesn't even have to be worn.
>
> Without this I might as well just keep wishing for Magicbane, which has
> engrave for backstab and curse protection.

The whole objection is that this lets any altar become early MR
(meaning you don't have to wait for a wish).

In other words, those (including me) who think it's way overpowered
_do_ want you to have to spend a wish to get Magicbane or GDSM or
whatever rather than just have MR handed to you early on.

In designing any new class sac gift/starting object/skill it's
probably worth asking yourself "does this item dramatically change
what I would wish for in the pre-Castle game?"  If yes, then it's a
reasonable red flag--the proposal is likely too powerful, as you're
basically saying that this is a reasonable replacement for the most
useful item you can think of (or at least for much of that item's
worth).



